    test: make user modify assertion subid-independent
    
    plugin/test_interruptor.py::TestUserRules::test_user_modify_rule_wraps_in_unshare
    asserted `result.modified.startswith(f"{unshare_prefix()}'")` — an expectation
    derived from the same helper that builds the payload, so it pinned no contract
    of its own. The QA row's literal legacy prefix ("unshare --user --pid --fork
    --kill-child=SIGKILL bash -c ") is red on every host that selects the uid-mapped
    launch, which userns.unshare_prefix() emits whenever /etc/subuid and /etc/subgid
    carry a range for the caller.
    
    Replace it with a contract assertion (`_assert_sandboxed_modify`) that:
    
    * accepts BOTH legitimate launch spellings — the mapping-less legacy prefix and
      the uid-mapped prefix (`--map-users=65534:<subid>:1 --map-groups=… -S 65534
      -G 65534`) — so the test no longer depends on the host's subordinate-ID
      configuration or on which launch the host selects;
    * pins what is NOT host state: `--pid --fork --kill-child=SIGKILL bash -c `
      present, in order, immediately before the payload introducer;
    * pins the payload as the original command wrapped in ONE quoted argument, so a
      missing/incorrect contract, a bare `unshare`, an unquoted or truncated payload
      and a map range longer than one subordinate ID are all still rejected;
    * never hard-codes a subordinate-ID number (fixtures are DEFAULT_SUBID_START and
      two arbitrary values that are not this host's /etc/subuid entry).
    
    The `result.rule_id == "user-modify-danger-tool"` provenance assertion is kept.
    
    Tests added: both launch shapes accepted (3 mapped-ID fixtures), this host's own
    prefix whichever it is plus both prefixes rebuilt from userns, a regression pin
    that the pre-fix literal prefix is no longer required, 12 rejected malformed
    launches and a payload-less MODIFY result.
    
    Evidence — host has subuid/subgid ranges (kara:100000:65536 in both files) but is
    AppArmor-degraded, so unshare_prefix() returns the mapping-less form:
    * focused test 1 passed; whole file 405 passed; full suite 880 passed / 5
      skipped; `uvx ruff check plugin/test_interruptor.py` clean.
    * mapped-capable host simulated with a test-only launch-runner double
      (`-p tj_mapped_host`; no production file touched): the rewrite becomes
      `unshare --user --map-users=65534:100000:1 --map-groups=65534:100000:1
      -S 65534 -G 65534 --pid --fork --kill-child=SIGKILL bash -c 'danger-tool
      --wipe'`; the pre-fix literal assertion returns False on it (the reported
      defect) while the new contract assertion passes (38 passed there).
    * mutation RED: (1) restricting the helper to the mapping-less shape fails 5 of
      the new tests; (2) weakening the payload check to `command in payload` makes
      the "unquoted payload" / "truncated payload" negatives stop raising. Both
      mutations were reverted; the committed file is byte-identical to the verified
      copy (sha256 74ad01f960a061e0a655175bb85de9dbeb3a23f58612ef9e11f4f2cb63bcd59e).
    
    Test-only change: plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/userns.py, the decider and
    every other production file are untouched.
    
    Addresses QA-TERMINAL-JAIL-8
    
